// #763 / harc#769 — runtime coverage for an ALWAYS-ON `hookable` method
// called on a `passive` DUT-poking transactor instance.
//
// #763 ("Support passive unbound transactor state") keeps a passive
// instance's always-on state AND its always-on handlers, hiding only the
// `when active` method surface. Its unit test only inspects the emitted
// C++ text, so the runtime path was never exercised — and it hid a
// miscompile (harc#769): the TB-IR emitter skipped ALL method lambdas for
// a passive-only transactor type (a pre-#763 "passive ⇒ no callable
// methods" assumption), emitting the call `CountPoker_bump(p)` with no
// definition. v1 emitted the definition and ran. This fixture drives the
// path so the two backends are trace-diffed.
//
// Coverage delta vs `passive_multi_instance_test` (which proves only that a
// passive instance's `default` state INITIALIZES and STAYS put, nothing
// poking it): here an always-on `hookable bump()` — declared OUTSIDE
// `when active`, so it survives on a passive instance — is CALLED on the
// passive instance and must UPDATE the always-on state at runtime. The
// `when active` `poke()` stays structurally unavailable and is never called.
//
// Self-check: state starts at its nonzero `default` (7), each always-on
// `bump()` increments it. v1 and TB-IR must agree (equivalence-gated).
domain SysDomain
  freq_mhz: 100
end domain SysDomain

transactor CountPoker
    dut : Top
    count : uint<32> default 7

    // Always-on handler (outside `when active`): kept on a passive instance.
    // Per spec §8.1 an always-on hookable body must NOT drive a DUT signal
    // (it would still execute on a passive instance), so it only mutates the
    // transactor's own always-on state.
    hookable bump()
        count = count + 1
    end bump

    when active
        // Active-only surface: absent on a passive instance. May drive the
        // DUT because it never runs on a passive instance.
        hookable poke()
            count = count + 100
            dut.en = 1
        end poke
    end when
end transactor CountPoker

testbench PassiveStateUpdateTb
    dut : Top
    p : CountPoker passive
end testbench PassiveStateUpdateTb

impl PassiveStateUpdateTest for PassiveStateUpdateTb
    clock clk = SysDomain
    run
        dut.rst = 1
        dut.en = 0
        wait 2 cycles
        dut.rst = 0

        // Always-on initial state is observable at runtime.
        assert p.count == 7 else fail("passive always-on state default lost: ${p.count}")

        // Always-on handler fires on a passive instance and updates state.
        p.bump()
        wait 1 cycle
        assert p.count == 8 else fail("always-on bump did not update passive state: ${p.count}")

        p.bump()
        wait 1 cycle
        assert p.count == 9 else fail("second always-on bump lost: ${p.count}")

        wait 3 cycles
        log(info, "ALL TESTS PASSED - passive transactor always-on state update")
    end run
end impl PassiveStateUpdateTest
